# gujiconform -- Phase 2 (Platform IO pass): `stdin` is the always-open
# standard-input handle (Section 15.4), a Handle value (not a function). It is
# read with the same `slurp` verb as a file handle: stdin.slurp() returns ALL of
# stdin VERBATIM (line terminators intact, no chomp). `stdin` references share a
# single underlying stream, so a second slurp after the input is consumed yields
# "". The expected output is derived from the spec, never captured from native.
sub main() {
    print("first:[" ~ stdin.slurp() ~ "]")
    print("second:[" ~ stdin.slurp() ~ "]")
}
